description:
The human asked at about 19:25Z on 2026-11-05: "can we use copilot as agents? (like a V in config ui use co pilot)".

Today the providers are claude, codex, gemini (Antigravity agy) and grok. moe-agent.sh:632-643 types any other command as claude, and the ps1 twin does the same. So "Custom…" with `copilot` gets claude's argv and cannot run. Copilot shows up only in docs/PRD.md:240, as "Autocomplete only".

Want: GitHub's agentic Copilot CLI (`copilot`, npm @github/copilot) as a selectable provider:
- in the JetBrains Agents menu, AgentProvider in TerminalAgentLauncher.kt, and agentCommand settings, with VS Code parity;
- launched by both wrappers one-shot and headless per task, with the moe proxy and Serena MCP servers written in the CLI's own MCP config format;
- with worker.type COPILOT end to end (MOE_WORKER_TYPE, the daemon, the board).

The plan must settle these against the INSTALLED CLI (verify the flags, as for grok and agy). `copilot` is NOT installed on this host, in Windows or in WSL, so the human installs it and signs in (a GitHub Copilot subscription) before any real-CLI smoke:
- the headless prompt and permission flags, and how MCP servers and env reach it;
- an argv probe like codex's (MOE_CLI_ARGV_REJECTED, never a relaunch loop);
- auth detection;
- whether its output gives a TOOL witness for landing attribution (else it lands like Gemini and Grok);
- the model and effort settings.
Known limits:
- Verified-local VM seats run only claude and codex, so a copilot worker or QA seat is refused there (MOE_VERIFIED_LOCAL_CLI_UNSUPPORTED) unless the plan says otherwise.
- Claude account rotation does not apply.
- Keep sh and ps1 in string parity.

Edges: dependsOn slice B (task-98053b89), which also edits moe-agent.{sh,ps1}. Size: split with moe-epic-breakdown if the wrappers, plugins and docs exceed one task.

implementationPlan.description:
Docs, with the Edit tool, taking every string from the landed wrappers and IDE code (no placeholder text).
docs/CONFIGURATION.md:
- the :43 MOE_WORKER_TYPE row: (`CLAUDE`, `CODEX`, `GEMINI`, `GROK` or `COPILOT`);
- the :55 row: `copilot` → `COPILOT` before 'anything else → `CLAUDE`';
- the :84 MOE_DISABLE_ARGV_PROBE row: the probe covers codex and copilot. Quote copilot's measured rejections, `error: unexpected argument '<flag>' found` and `error: invalid value '<v>' for '--reasoning-effort <level>'`;
- new rows MOE_COPILOT_MODEL and MOE_COPILOT_EFFORT beside MOE_GROK_MODEL/MOE_GROK_EFFORT, with the landed precedence. Model: --model/-Model > settings.models.{role} > MOE_COPILOT_MODEL > copilot's own default, never the claude fallback. Effort: MOE_COPILOT_EFFORT > the claimed task's launch effort > no flag;
- the :201 agentCommand row: add `copilot` to the values. Say it is GitHub Copilot CLI: `npm install -g @github/copilot`, then `copilot login`, separately on Windows and in WSL; the account needs Copilot CLI and MCP servers allowed. Add it to the protected list too: `claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `grok` or `copilot`, matching JetBrains' landed enum-derived allowlist and the wrappers' MOE_PROTECTED_AGENT_COMMAND_REFUSED line;
- the :226 models.{role} row: copilot takes it as --model (absent: MOE_COPILOT_MODEL, else copilot's default).
docs/SCHEMA.md: in the NOTE under WorkerType (about :1179-1180; a8e13516's 2026-11-05 22:11Z comment), the CLI list becomes `CLAUDE, CODEX, GEMINI, GROK or COPILOT (any other command is CLAUDE)`.
docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md: add a `### Copilot seat stops with a MOE_COPILOT_* or MOE_CLI_ARGV_REJECTED line` section after the two Codex sections, before `## Task Sync Issues`, plus its Table of Contents entry. Give one short entry per code, with the exact landed line and its fix:
- MOE_COPILOT_NOT_FOUND: install it on that OS (`npm install -g @github/copilot`; Windows and WSL separately; an IDE-launched seat needs it on the IDE's PATH).
- MOE_COPILOT_SIGNED_OUT: `copilot login` on that OS, or COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN. WSL keeps the token in plaintext ~/.copilot/config.json.
- MOE_COPILOT_NOT_ENTITLED: `Access denied by policy settings`, logged as HTTP 403 `not authorized to use this Copilot feature`. The account's plan lacks Copilot CLI, or its organization disabled it (github.com/settings/copilot).
- MOE_COPILOT_MCP_BLOCKED: `Third-party MCP servers are disabled by your organization's Copilot policy` or `MCP server was blocked by policy`. Moe's moe and serena servers are local stdio servers, so the policy must allow MCP servers, and no registry allowlist may exclude them.
- MOE_COPILOT_CONFIG_FAILED: the wrapper could not write its private prompt or MCP file (the temp dir is full or not writable).
- MOE_CLI_ARGV_REJECTED for copilot: version drift between the plugin and copilot. Reinstall the plugin or pin copilot; MOE_DISABLE_ARGV_PROBE=1 skips the check.

acceptanceCriteria:
The docs cover:
- scripts/CLAUDE.md: the per-CLI copilot paragraph, and copilot in the TOOL-tier and MCP-servers bullets;
- CONFIGURATION.md: agentCommand, models.{role}, both MOE_WORKER_TYPE rows, MOE_DISABLE_ARGV_PROBE, MOE_COPILOT_MODEL and MOE_COPILOT_EFFORT;
- SCHEMA.md: the launcher NOTE;
- TROUBLESHOOTING.md: a copilot section;
- README and PRD (task-1c580985): checked by the gate.

sourceAssumptions:
Measured on copilot 1.0.106 in WSL (mem:decision-copilot-cli-contract):
- the slice argv parses (--help exits 0);
- rejections read `error: unexpected argument '<f>' found` and `error: invalid value '<v>' for '--reasoning-effort <level>'`;
- with no prompt it prints `No prompt provided...`;
- signed out, stderr says `Error: No authentication information found.` and the log holds `[ERROR] No authentication information found.`;
- the human's account gets `Access denied by policy settings` (log: 403 `not authorized to use this Copilot feature`) and `Third-party MCP servers are disabled by your organization's Copilot policy`, the latter on stderr only.
